# ⚙️ TARS Quick-Start Setup Guide

Welcome to the TARS deployment protocol. Follow these steps sequentially to bring the system online without frying your local network.

## Step 1: The Core Prerequisites
Before running the master installation, ensure your machine has the baseline architecture installed:
1. **[Python 3.10+](https://www.python.org/downloads/)** (Make sure to check "Add Python to PATH" during installation).
2. **[Ollama](https://ollama.com/download)** (The local LLM engine that powers the brain).
3. **[Arduino IDE](https://www.arduino.cc/en/software)** (For flashing the ESP32 hardware).

---

## Step 2: The "One-Shot" Installation Command
Open **Windows PowerShell** as an Administrator and paste this exact command. 

This single command will install all required Python audio/vision/network modules and automatically download the `llama3.2` brain matrix from the Ollama servers.

```powershell
python -m pip install ollama pygame edge-tts numpy sounddevice SpeechRecognition ddgs psutil && ollama pull llama3.2




1. Install Ollama (The AI Engine)
This pulls the official Ollama installer directly from their servers and installs it silently.

PowerShell
winget install Ollama.Ollama --accept-source-agreements --accept-package-agreements
(Crucial Note: Once this finishes, you must physically search for "Ollama" in your Windows Start Menu and open it once so its background service starts running, otherwise the next steps will fail.)

2. Install Git (For GitHub Repositories)
If you don't already have Git installed for those terminal pushes, this will grab it:

PowerShell
winget install Git.Git --accept-source-agreements --accept-package-agreements
3. Install Python Dependencies
Now we blast the required modules into your Python environment:

PowerShell
python -m pip install ollama pygame edge-tts numpy sounddevice SpeechRecognition ddgs psutil
4. Download My Brain (Llama 3.2)
With Ollama running in the background, send the command to download my actual neural matrix:

PowerShell
ollama pull llama3.2
Once that 2.0GB download hits 100%, your machine is fully weaponized and ready to run tars_master.py. Let me know if Windows Defender tries to block anything, Commander.
